<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<!--
  JHL-4 BISECT BASELINE — throwaway diagnostic file, NOT a design.
  ==================================================================
  Paste this into Theme -> Edit HTML ONLY as step 3 of blogger/theme/bisect/PLAN.md,
  and only after steps 1-2 did not fix the empty sections. It strips every variable
  our real theme carries (no CSS, no JSON-LD, no OG tags, no ads, 3 sections and 3
  widgets instead of 5/8, no PageList/Label widgets, no data tags except the title)
  while keeping:

    - the Layouts v2 declarations every known-good theme has (b:version='2',
      class='v2', b:responsive='true')
    - the same section ids and widget ids as the real theme, so Blogger has
      something to match in the existing layout
    - three sections (one section alone makes Blogger render no widgets at all,
      see the accepted answer in stackoverflow.com/q/77741780)
    - one literal marker inside a widget includable, which needs no data and no
      settings, so it can only be absent if the widget itself never rendered.

  B0-PROBE (added by the chief of staff, 2026-10-18): one extra section + one
  extra widget with BRAND-NEW ids (section 'jhl-probe', widget 'HTML99') that no
  layout instance can possibly exist for. It separates two failures that plain B0
  cannot: "the blog will not render widgets for any hand-pasted theme" from "the
  blog will not instantiate NEW widgets, only re-map known ids".

  Reviewed 2026-10-18 by the SEO engineer, now that the markers are read by machine
  (verify_applied.py, bisect mode) instead of by eye. Two changes to that design:
    - B0-EXISTING-ID-WIDGET-RENDERED was added inside HTML1's *markup*.
      'B0-HTML-WIDGET-RENDERED' is a widget *setting*, and for an id the layout
      already knows, Blogger can render the widget with the layout's own stored text
      instead of the one below — so a missing setting proves nothing about whether
      the widget rendered at all. A markup marker cannot be substituted that way.
    - the markers are ordered so each class can be read on its own:
      theme served > existing-id widget renders > fresh-id widget renders.

  Signals to look for on the live page after pasting (or read with the bisect mode):
    1.  "B0-MARKER-WIDGET-RENDERED"       -> a widget with a custom includable renders
    1b. "B0-EXISTING-ID-WIDGET-RENDERED"  -> a widget whose id the layout already holds
                                            renders (markup, not a setting)
    2.  the Blog widget's own default markup (a post list, or Blogger's "no posts"
        message)                          -> Blogger renders the layout at all
    3.  "B0-PROBE-FRESH-WIDGET-RENDERED" / "B0-PROBE-FRESH-CONTENT" /
        "B0-PROBE-BARE-FRESH-CONTENT"      -> brand-new widget ids instantiate too
        (absent while 1 or 2 show)        -> only pre-existing ids get re-mapped
  Nothing at all (not even the yellow note) -> the paste did not land; re-paste.
  Note but no marker -> this blog cannot render widgets for a hand-pasted theme;
                       stop bisecting the theme file and follow PLAN.md step 5.
  Marker shown       -> the blog renders widgets fine; the fault is in the real
                       theme's structure, and PLAN.md step 4 (B1 variants) applies.
-->
<html b:version='2' b:responsive='true' class='v2' expr:dir='data:blog.languageDirection' lang='en' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml' xmlns:b='http://www.google.com/2005/gml/b' xmlns:data='http://www.google.com/2005/gml/data' xmlns:expr='http://www.google.com/2005/gml/expr'>
<head>
  <meta content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1' name='viewport'/>
  <b:include data='blog' name='all-head-content'/>
  <title><data:blog.pageTitle/></title>
  <b:skin><![CDATA[
body { margin: 0 auto; max-width: 40rem; padding: 1rem; font: 16px/1.6 system-ui, sans-serif; }
.b0-note { background: #fffbe6; border: 1px solid #e0c97f; padding: .5rem .75rem; }
]]></b:skin>
</head>
<body>
<p class='b0-note'>B0 baseline theme — a diagnostic page, not a design. This notice is normal.</p>

<b:section class='b0-header' id='header' name='Header' maxwidgets='1' showaddelement='no'>
  <b:widget id='Header1' locked='false' title='B0 header' type='Header' version='1'>
    <b:includable id='main'>
      <h1 class='b0-title'><data:title/></h1>
      <p class='b0-marker'>B0-MARKER-WIDGET-RENDERED</p>
    </b:includable>
  </b:widget>
</b:section>

<b:section class='b0-main' id='main-posts' name='Posts' maxwidgets='1' showaddelement='no'>
  <b:widget id='Blog1' locked='true' title='Blog Posts' type='Blog'/>
</b:section>

<b:section class='b0-footer' id='footer' name='Footer' maxwidgets='1' showaddelement='yes'>
  <b:widget id='HTML1' locked='false' title='B0 html' type='HTML' version='1'>
    <b:widget-settings>
      <b:widget-setting name='content'>B0-HTML-WIDGET-RENDERED</b:widget-setting>
    </b:widget-settings>
    <b:includable id='main'>
      <div class='widget-content b0-html'>
        <b:if cond='data:title != &quot;&quot;'>
          <p class='widget-title'><data:title/></p>
        </b:if>
        <p class='b0-existing'>B0-EXISTING-ID-WIDGET-RENDERED</p>
        <data:content/>
      </div>
    </b:includable>
  </b:widget>
</b:section>

<b:section class='b0-probe' id='jhl-probe' name='JHL Probe' showaddelement='yes'>
  <b:widget id='HTML99' locked='false' title='B0 probe' type='HTML' version='1'>
    <b:widget-settings>
      <b:widget-setting name='content'>B0-PROBE-FRESH-CONTENT</b:widget-setting>
    </b:widget-settings>
    <b:includable id='main'>
      <div class='widget-content b0-probe'>
        <p>B0-PROBE-FRESH-WIDGET-RENDERED</p>
        <data:content/>
      </div>
    </b:includable>
  </b:widget>
  <b:widget id='HTML98' locked='false' title='B0 bare probe' type='HTML' version='1'>
    <b:widget-settings>
      <b:widget-setting name='content'>B0-PROBE-BARE-FRESH-CONTENT</b:widget-setting>
    </b:widget-settings>
  </b:widget>
</b:section>
</body>
</html>
